### **Problem 2: Unmigrated Columns in Existing PostgreSQL / SQLite Tables**
```
get_user_documents error: column "summary" does not exist
LINE 2: ... SELECT filename, size_bytes, page_count, status, summary, c...
```

### **Root Cause**:
`CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` is a no-op if the table was created by an older version of the codebase. Adding new columns to queries without migrating existing tables causes queries to fail.

### **Prevention Rule**:
```sql
-- ❌ WRONG - Assuming CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS updates schema
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS documents (...);

-- ✅ CORRECT - Run idempotent column migrations on startup
ALTER TABLE documents ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS summary TEXT;
ALTER TABLE documents ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS chunk_count INT DEFAULT 0;
ALTER TABLE documents ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS error TEXT;
```
